# relay enable/disable/restart verb scoping: restart ignores relay.json and inverts URL precedence; enable writes repo-local config under broker env

## Steps to Reproduce

1. TODO: Add steps

## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

Two verb-scoping defects. (1) c2c restart relay-connect bootstrap resolves first_nonempty_url [override; env] then [saved config; override; env] (c2c_relay_managed.ml:461-499) - relay.json/Relay_activation is never a candidate, so on an enable-only non-systemd host restart errors "no relay URL known" even though start works, and when saved config.json holds a URL it WINS over C2C_RELAY_URL - inverted precedence vs start/connect (B300/B242); re-pointing via relay enable --url followed by restart relaunches on the stale URL. (2) enable/disable write through config_location which honors C2C_RELAY_CONFIG/C2C_MCP_BROKER_ROOT: enable inside a broker-scoped session writes the repo-local relay.json; a later plain-shell disable writes enabled:false to the MACHINE file and stops the unit, but the repo-local file still resolves active so relay status/monitor/dm in that repo keep phoning the relay the operator believes is off.

## Fix direction

restart bootstrap: add Relay_activation.url () as last candidate, order override > env > activation > saved-config-once. enable/disable: print or refuse without --config when config_location () is not the machine config; disable warns when a repo-local relay.json still resolves active.

## Evidence

CLI review 2026-09-17 (merges findings 8+9).